author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 150
acceptance_criteria: Failed replacement restores prior files and exact managed/settings bytes; prior commands work in a fresh process; failures report previous_state_preserved and actionable recovery; successful and fresh installs retain their contracts
parent: pm-ugqx
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Keep a recoverable snapshot through persistence and runtime verification; restore rejected copied replacements, preserve audited settings history, retain concrete recovery sources on rollback failure, propagate receipts and expose typed public SDK diagnostics."
expected_result: "A rejected replacement preserves the prior code settings and managed bytes, old commands remain usable, and failures disclose truthful preservation and executable recovery evidence."
actual_result: "All147 linked replacement and existing extension/discovery cases pass, public root/runtime consumer type fixtures and four TypeScript projects pass, identical unchanged-main negative controls reject the original behavior, and all14 native partitions plus exact100/100/100/100 aggregate pass in Nightly39776721982. Typed reserved-field migration is documented and explicitly acknowledged. Delivery is reviewed in PR1548; this does not claim a new registry publication."
